  "title": "Three Quays",
  "rules": [
    "Each merchant initially owns goods that another merchant needs.",
    "Carry one owned or publicly gifted good at a time through the shared corridors.",
    "Deposit cargo on your own escrow pad and commit to a visible recipient for three ticks.",
    "A compatible complete two-party or three-party cycle transfers ownership only after every offer matures.",
    "Settled cargo stays at its real pad. Its new owner must collect and deliver it.",
    "Mature offers can be withdrawn at the seller's pad; public gifts can be claimed without a reciprocal promise."
